  "how_definitions": {
    "call_direct": "callee() by bare name",
    "call_self": "self.callee() / cls.callee()",
    "call_super": "super().callee()",
    "call_attr_other": "obj.callee() on any other object",
    "instantiation": "Callee() where the callee is a class (or a collapsed __init__)",
    "call_in_nested_scope": "explicit call, but inside a def/class nested in the caller",
    "referenced": "name used without a call (callback, decorator, passed, assigned)",
    "implicit_dunder": "callee is a dunder method and nothing in the caller names it",
    "text_only": "name appears only in a string or comment of the caller",
    "no_reference": "the caller's own code does not mention the callee at all",
    "caller_not_found": "caller node id not located in the snapshot"
  },
  "notes": "Unconfirmed edges with an explicit callsite are plausible calls that the tests did not run (or a name match to a same-named method of another class). no_reference / text_only unconfirmed edges are spurious. Compare callee_name_shared_share across populations: a name-matching generator inflates it for unconfirmed edges relative to captured ones."
}